* =====================================================================
* Behavioural op-amp macromodel (written for this repository; no vendor code).
* Pins (our convention): inp inn vcc vee out
* Values in the wrappers come from the manufacturers' datasheets; see
* models/README.md for every value, its source page and the assumptions.
*
* Structure:
*  - input: RIN between the inputs, IB bias current into each input
*  - transconductance stage with a smooth current limit (tanh) into an
*    integrator C||R referenced to mid-supply:
*        GBW = GM/(2*pi*C),  AOL = GM*R,  SR = IMAX/C
*    (the tanh input range IMAX/GM = SR/(2*pi*GBW) is ~50 mV, like a
*    bipolar differential pair)
*  - the integrator node is clamped by two sharp diodes to vcc-VDROP and
*    vee+VDROP (anti-windup), buffered, then ROUT in series with the output
* Not modelled: offset, input common-mode limits, noise, supply current,
* second poles, temperature.
* =====================================================================
.subckt OPAMP_MACRO inp inn vcc vee out
+ params: AOL=1e5 GBW=3e6 SR=1e6 VDROP=1.9 ROUT=50 IB=25n RIN=5Meg
.param CC=1n
.param GM={2*3.14159265358979*GBW*CC}
.param RG={AOL/GM}
.param IMAX={SR*CC}
Rin  inp inn {RIN}
Ibp  inp vee {IB}
Ibn  inn vee {IB}
Bmid mid 0 V = (V(vcc)+V(vee))/2
Bgm  mid g I = {IMAX}*tanh({GM}*(V(inp)-V(inn))/{IMAX})
Cc   g mid {CC}
Rg   g mid {RG}
* anti-windup / output limit: sharp diode clamps to the rails minus VDROP
Bhi  hi 0 V = V(vcc)-{VDROP}
Blo  lo 0 V = V(vee)+{VDROP}
Dhi  g hi DCLAMP
Dlo  lo g DCLAMP
.model DCLAMP D(Is=1e-15 N=0.1)
Bout o 0 V = V(g)
Rout o out {ROUT}
.ends OPAMP_MACRO

* NJM4558 (one half), Nisshinbo NJM4558 datasheet Ver. 20260723:
*   AV 100 dB, GB 3 MHz, SR 1 V/us, IB 25 nA, RIN 5 MOhm (p.2);
*   swing 2 V from each rail at RL=2k, constant vs supply (p.2 table, p.4 graph).
*   ROUT 50 Ohm is an assumption (not in the datasheet); VDROP is set so that
*   the lowest graph point is met: +-6 V supply, RL=2k -> +-4.0 V (1.9 + 50*2 mA = 2.0 V)
.subckt JRC4558_HALF inp inn vcc vee out
X1 inp inn vcc vee out OPAMP_MACRO AOL=1e5 GBW=3e6 SR=1e6 VDROP=1.9 ROUT=50 IB=25n RIN=5Meg
.ends JRC4558_HALF

* LM741, TI datasheet SNOSC25D (rev. Oct 2015):
*   AVOL 200 V/mV, SR 0.5 V/us, IB 80 nA, ri 2 MOhm, swing +-13 V at RL>=2k (p.5);
*   GBW 1.17 MHz = 0.35 / rise time 0.3 us (p.5), formula from p.6 note (2).
*   No swing-vs-supply graph: constant headroom assumed. ROUT 50 Ohm assumed; VDROP set
*   so that +-15 V, RL=2k -> +-13 V (1.675 + 50*6.5 mA = 2.0 V).
*   Note: recommended supply is +-10 V minimum (p.4); a 9 V pedal is outside that range.
.subckt LM741 inp inn vcc vee out
X1 inp inn vcc vee out OPAMP_MACRO AOL=2e5 GBW=1.17e6 SR=0.5e6 VDROP=1.675 ROUT=50 IB=80n RIN=2Meg
.ends LM741
